# 65-vu1-opstat-chain-diag: measurement only. GOW_VU1_OPSTAT=1 counts the dynamic opcode mix per VU1 program entry;
# GOW_VU1_COST=1 now also splits VU1NativeAccess::chain out of the dispatch loop and says which entry-timing path a block
# takes. Off by default (one static branch per block / per run while unset).
#
# Why: patch 63 says the VU1 wall is three microprograms (pc 0 / 18 / 30) but not what their code is made of, and patch 62
# put the whole remaining share in "blockcode". The pair classes come from the exact engine's decoder, once per block; every
# execution adds the block's static counts, so the sums are exact pair counts, not a sample, and must match patch 63's
# `pairs` for the same entry (0.3 % here, the 5 s window offset of the two reports).
#
# Measured (i3-4170 + HD 4400, Asia disc, 0.5x, GOW_VU1_FAST=1, -Scripted attract demo, 70 s, 5 s windows; three
# consecutive windows agree within 1 %):
#   pairs 250-258M per 5 s. Upper: FMAC 30.8-31.9 %, FMAC writing ACC 29.7-30.8 %, special (ITOF/FTOI/ABS/CLIP) 14.5-14.6 %,
#   NOP 21.2-23.1 %, I-bit 1.6-1.7 %. Lower: IALU 33.7-34.7 %, memory (LQ/SQ/LQI/SQI/ILW/ISW) 27.3-27.6 %, branch 12.6-12.9 %,
#   FDIV 2.2-2.4 %, EFU 0.2 %, XGKICK 0.1 %, NOP 18.5-20.2 %, special-register moves 3.4-3.8 %.
#   Flag writers (ADD/SUB/MADD/MSUB) 41.4-43.0 %, ACC readers 46.7-48.4 %, status-op reads (FSxx) 0.0 %, WAITQ 0.1 %.
#   Branches: static (B/BAL) 2.1 %, dynamic (JR/JALR) 0.6-0.8 %, conditional (IBEQ..IBGEZ) 9.9-10.1 % - so a superblock
#   across static branches could reach at most 2 % of the pairs.
#   chain: 6.4-6.6M calls/s at ~140-160 ns per block body; the 1/16 rdtsc sample of chain reads 68-72 ns per call (noise
#   included), 43-48 % of block time. 99 % of chained blocks read entry flags, 52 % carry a tail, 19 % touch scalar
#   pipelines, 1 % take the self-loop path. [vu1-bt]: memo 99.6 %, idle 0.4 %, cache 0.0 %, sim 0.0 % - the entry-flag
#   timing is a memo hit, so the flag latency model itself is not a cost.
